course: dictionary
lesson: 5245
title: Jittery and the feelings in words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Jittery is a feeling word. It means nervous and shaky, like the wobbly hands you get before a big test or a race. «Before the spelling test, Maya felt jittery and kept dropping her pencil.» Dropping her pencil and feeling wobbly show that jittery means shaky with nerves.
explain: Jittery can also come from caffeine, a substance found in coffee. «Too much caffeine can make people jittery, give them a fast heartbeat and stop them sleeping well.» So a person can feel jittery from worry, or because they have had too much caffeine.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put «nervous and shaky» in place of jittery: «Before the spelling test, Maya felt nervous and shaky and kept dropping her pencil.» It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
fact: «Jittery» means nervous and shaky.
fact: People often feel jittery when they are worried, such as before a test, a show or a race.
fact: Caffeine, found in coffee, can make people jittery, give them a fast heartbeat and stop them sleeping well.
fact: «Jittery» is an adjective, so it can change to jitterier and jitteriest when you compare things.
fact: «Jittery» is an informal word, so you will hear it in everyday talk more than in formal writing.
exercise: «Before the race, Sam felt jittery and could not keep still.» What does jittery mean? | Very tired and sleepy | Angry with his friends | Calm and relaxed | *Nervous and shaky
exercise: «Too much caffeine can make people jittery, give them a fast heartbeat and stop them sleeping well.» Which thing can make people jittery? | *Too much caffeine | Sleeping well | Cold weather | Going to bed early
exercise: Which word means the same as jittery? | Relaxed | *Nervous | Cheerful | Sleepy
test: «Lily was so jittery before the race that she could not tie her shoes.» Why was Lily jittery? | *Because she was nervous about the race | Because she was relaxed and calm | Because she was asleep | Because it was raining
test: Which word describes someone who is shaky and nervous before a show? | *Jittery | Calm | Cheerful | Sleepy
exam: «Coffee can make people jittery, so it is not good for children.» What does jittery mean here? | Hungry | Very clean | Happy and bouncy | *Nervous and shaky
